or, six powers from Sensitive and Physical, no exceptions. The page prints no I.S.P.; isp_base is the stored crazy''s formula under the unless-otherwise-noted rule. || P.P.E.: the page prints none and the RUE crazy''s 6D6 is not a power, so ppe_base is not stated. || SKILLS: Mathematics: Basic 45+10, Japanese (+20%) as Language: Native Tongue at 98% (the bonus cannot raise the native figure), Literacy: Japanese as Literacy: Native Language 40+15, Computer Operation 40+5, Computer Programming 30+5, Computer Hacking 15+10, Climbing 40+10+12, Prowl 25+10+12 (the +12% of power 4), Pick Locks 30+10+10 and Demolitions 60+10+10 (the +10% delicate touch of power 4). W.P. three of choice. || HAND TO HAND: Assassin, replaceable by Aikido, Jujitsu or Karate at no cost; Ninjitsu not available, so costs are aikido, jujitsu and karate at 0. || RELATED: eight, at least two Rogue (minimums), plus one at levels 4, 8 and 12. Mechanical is split into two entries so the +10% reaches Locksmith only. Criminal Science & Forensics is the catalog''s Forensics. || SECONDARY: six from the same list, limits kept, no bonuses. || EQUIPMENT: micro-film camera and small crowbar as this book''s micro-film-camera and small-crowbar rows (printed 83); knotted rope as 50 x climbing-rope-per-foot; nondescript clothing and disguises as clothing. The energy weapon, vibro-blade and ancient weapon are of choice and the from lists are the catalog''s Rifts Japan sets. Tracer chip granted as the tracer-chip row; the clan-ordered implants sentence above the Ninja Crazy heading on printed 86 is the Ninja Juicer''s, not this class''s. || MONEY: 2D6x1000 credits stored; the 1D4x1000 in black market salable items is prose (side_effects)."
---

## Lore

Some tech-ninja clans use M.O.M. brain implants to make modern counterparts of the ninja of old. Like the ninja juicers, candidates come from the young trainees raised in the clans'' hidden camps, picked for high mental endurance and intelligence, and taught meditation to hold back the insanity the implants cause. Latent and minor psychics are preferred and their gifts are cultivated, so a ninja crazy resists his madness better than an untrained crazy and commands twice the psionic powers, enough to rival the traditional ninja in the mystic arts.

The ninja crazy is above all a thief, expert at every kind of breaking and entering from cat burglary to safe-cracking and demolitions; when something must be stolen, a paired team of a tech-ninja and a ninja crazy goes to get it. His psychic powers serve eavesdropping and deceit. Combat and assassination come second: the clans rank their killers ''borgs first, juicers second, crazies third and ordinary tech-ninja fourth, and assign ranks by the danger of the mission.

## The Buddy System

Visible implants and erratic behavior rule out long undercover work. Each crazy is paired with a tech-ninja trained in psychological techniques, usually a friend he trained beside, who calms him during episodes and watches his back; the pair are seldom split up. In the clan''s hidden safe-houses the crazy''s insanities are allowed free rein as long as no ninja gets hurt. A crazy whose sanity slips until he endangers the missions or the secrecy of the clans is eliminated, usually on the order of the jonin.

## GM Notes

The G.M. rolls the 3D4-day control period in secret. When it ends, the character saves vs psychic attack/insanity once per insanity, with the level bonuses and M.E. bonus, at -1 per day since his last meditation and therapy; each failed save lets that delusion take full force, which may or may not affect the mission. The Random Crazy Insanity Table (Frenzy, Power by Association, Multiple Personalities) is the American Crazy''s; see the Crazy O.C.C.

The equipment section describes other specialized ninja gear; the G.M. decides whether a character starts with any of it.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ninja-crazy');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ninja-crazy';

